WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:01.780
There is milk in the fridge.

2
00:00:01.830 --> 00:00:04.240
Open the door, and you can check.

3
00:00:04.290 --> 00:00:06.670
All bachelors are unmarried.

4
00:00:06.720 --> 00:00:09.580
That one is true just
by what the words mean.

5
00:00:09.630 --> 00:00:15.560
In 1936, the philosopher A J Ayer argued
that a statement only has meaning if

6
00:00:15.610 --> 00:00:18.240
it passes one of these two tests.

7
00:00:18.290 --> 00:00:22.260
Now try a moral sentence:
stealing is wrong.

8
00:00:22.310 --> 00:00:26.620
When you say it, are you stating
a fact, or showing how you feel?

9
00:00:26.670 --> 00:00:30.920
In this mission, you'll put moral
sentences through that test for meaning.

10
00:00:30.970 --> 00:00:34.250
Then you'll compare rival
answers and weigh them up.

11
00:00:34.300 --> 00:00:39.140
Your mission: work out what a moral
sentence is really doing when someone says

12
00:00:39.190 --> 00:00:39.470
it.
